# A napplet is published by the sha256 of its built artifact, so the build has to
# be byte-identical everywhere. Line endings are the usual way that quietly stops
# being true: check the same commit out on Windows with CRLF and every source file
# differs, the bundle differs, the hash differs, and the signed manifest no longer
# matches the blob. Normalise to LF in the repo and in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets get inlined as data URIs, so they must never be touched.
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary
